    {
      "id": "a7afa0e1af3d10f6f22c88b93e14530a20018345",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1129912605,
          "type": null,
          "body": "In practice, it's always initialized for QUIC as well (because the dissector registers it), but there should be a check for correctness sake.\n\nHowever, long term we should get rid of all the dissector specific code in the follow stream Qt code to make it easier to register new streams. So I think removing the different text is good, even though it makes the text more generic (QUIC \"streams\" like all other protocols instead of \"connections\".)\n\nBoth HTTP2 and QUIC have functions for finding the next higher and lower substream number than the current substream for a given stream. I intend to make those functions registered by the dissectors instead of special cases in the Qr code later too.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
